{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/80279-abusing-pacts-for-fun-and-profit","id":80279,"title":"Abusing Pacts for Fun and Profit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-26T09:02:15-08:00","id":80279,"title":"Abusing Pacts for Fun and Profit","content":"I'm going to run my first Demon game this friday, and I'm excited. So, I've been re-reading the rules all over again, trying to absorb everything. Then I got to the pact rules.<br /> <br /> I am seeing one abuse that is probably completely doable: <br /> <br /> The Demon makes a pact with someone desperate. The pactee will get what he wants (say, a 3 point pact). But, he will have to work for the Demon. But not without some other bennies.<br /> <br /> Mortal Benefits:<br /> - 3 point benefit for the mortal - let's say, +3 resources.<br /> - 3 point added benefit for the mortal - firearms 2.<br /> - 3 point added benefit for the mortal - +3 firearms.<br /> - 3 point added benefit for the mortal - 5 point gun training.<br /> <br /> Demon Benefits:<br /> - 3 point: permanent<br /> - 3 point: Retainer (the pactee). <br /> - 3 point: some cover points for the demon, why not?<br /> <br /> Total Demon cost: (9-9) = (minimum)1 wp.<br /> <br /> So, he can get superior retainers, permanently, for 1 wp each. Also, they have resources 5, what will also be useful. What I did for firearms, I can do for anything, basically. Does he want to have a Comissioner, Judge? Psychic wunderkind? The demon just can do it. <br /> <br /> I can just imagine some of my smartass players will try something like that, also. Is this valid? What should I do to block this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:43:46-08:00","id":80300,"title":"","content":"Not really the main problem, but I don't think you can have two pact benefits giving bonuses to the same skill. At least, that doesn't seem to be the intent.<br /> <br /> In general, the thing about pacts is that the mortal has to want to sign as well. They might be desperate, but the demon is still going to have to convince them that working for them (<i>serving </i>them, really) as a bodyguard/hitman/whatever, permanently, is a good idea. Granting skill at firearms will definitely help, but there might be other problems with the suitability of someone who's never been in a fight before, how their psyche will adjust, whether they're in good shape, etc. And the trouble with pacts with a demon is the mortal tends to get cold feet- what if you make your retainer do something they don't want to do, and they start devoting their incredible wealth and combat ability to covertly finding a way out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:00:48-08:00","id":80319,"title":"","content":"Well, not giving double skills is something, at least. But even if you can't give firearms 2 and then firearms 5, you can pick somebody with just 1 or 2 (for instance, security guards, criminals, etc), and give them +3. Which, combined with professional training at 5, and the maneuver packages, can be quite devastating. That also works for burnout employess, that can become CEOs in a week, or grunts than can become generals, and so on.<br /> <br /> And if your retainers start working against you, you rip their contracts. Now, they are harmless, and you didn't lose anything you can't replace quite easily (don't use the cover exp unless you really need them!). Of course, now they are cover liabilities, but they will quite vulnerable while their world crumbles around them, I suppose. <br /> <br /> It just seems so easy to get powerful retainers. Much easier and controllable than, say, using that stigmatic exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:23:16-08:00","id":80377,"title":"","content":"Oh, it is. Though do keep in mind, if you roll deep with a crew of multi-millionares with highly altered life stories, the first time the God Machine comes sniffing you're going to go up like a roman candle.<br /> <br /> Better to work -with- the machine ; don't just give money to a homeless guy and make him a ninja. Find a special forces operative. Slowly -nudge- people... in believable ways... to the roles you need them in. That way, when the Angel comes to check the paperwork, everything looks plausible.<br /> <br /> You -can- create a superagency filled with Bruce Waynes, just... it may not serve your purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T12:30:16-08:00","id":80430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/80279-abusing-pacts-for-fun-and-profit?p=80319#post80319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not giving double skills is something, at least. But even if you can't give firearms 2 and then firearms 5, you can pick somebody with just 1 or 2 (for instance, security guards, criminals, etc), and give them +3. Which, combined with professional training at 5, and the maneuver packages, can be quite devastating. That also works for burnout employess, that can become CEOs in a week, or grunts than can become generals, and so on.<br /> <br /> And if your retainers start working against you, you rip their contracts. Now, they are harmless, and you didn't lose anything you can't replace quite easily (don't use the cover exp unless you really need them!). Of course, now they are cover liabilities, but they will quite vulnerable while their world crumbles around them, I suppose.<br /> <br /> It just seems so easy to get powerful retainers. Much easier and controllable than, say, using that stigmatic exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, none of this plays out in a vacuum. With them being cover liabilities for instance, it would be on you as the ST to make something threaten the PCs because of that. Just in general, i'd say that letting the players' plans work out perfectly is boring for everybody because there's no challenge. If your players do show an interest in doing that, it might be a good idea to start setting them against heavily-defended facilities guarded by mortals whom the God-Machine has similarly altered into combat monsters and let them have at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:15:31-08:00","id":80830,"title":"","content":"So, &quot;Swear to serve me forever, and I shall grant you mortal powers beyond your wildest dreams!&quot;? That's not abuse, that's working as intended. Others have pointed out why you don't just run around doing that willy-nilly, but if you manage to pull it off, it's totally in-genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T05:45:33-08:00","id":80981,"title":"","content":"Well, then we have to know the effective reach of the God Machine. I suppose that if some CEOs started living together in a cult-like fashion, it would raise a lot of flags. But, you really don't have to do this with a CEO, or a judge. You let him live his life, and when you need something, you give him a call. As for skill-based pacts, it really depends how you set it up. If you take a zero to hero to walk with you as your bodyguard, it really depends on your cover. If you made a group of super-soldiers walking around you all the time, of course you're going to cal attention. But if you put them in, say, a militia, or even a new gang, and call them when you need them, that wouldn't raise many eyebrows. <br /> <br /> It may be somewhat in-genre to do that (demons generally make pacts for the afterlife, in general). But, I seek ways to not let pacts overwhelm other aspects of the game, and other mechanical aspects, such as social merits and certain expolits. I want to focus it more on the espionage and operatives, than on the 'pokemon' aspect (for lack of a better word).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}